{
  // Seasonal-mode-only task additions (pvp-season), merged after the shared
  // src/additions files.

  // Placeholder tasks (pvp-season, "Seasonal mode" on the wiki): quests the wiki
  // documents but no source exposes BSG task/objective IDs for yet. IDs are
  // synthetic and identity-based: task 'placeholder_<wiki title slug>',
  // objectives '<taskId>_objNN' in wiki order, so they never collide with 24-hex
  // BSG IDs. Every placeholder is tracked in
  // https://github.com/tarkovtracker-org/tarkov-data-overlay/issues/507; when a
  // real ID is known, replace the entry, record the placeholder -> real mapping
  // there and migrate stored progress (plan in the issue). Definitions come from
  // each linked wiki page. Map, item and trader references use real IDs.
  //
  // Gates are best-effort and placeholder-only: besides explicit "Unlocks N-M
  // after completion of X" Requirements lines, each placeholder is gated on its
  // wiki infobox `previous` quest (status ['active', 'complete'] when the wiki
  // says "Accept X", so finishing X keeps the gate met; else 'complete').
  // AGENTS.md treats `previous` as narrative order, not proof; it is used here
  // only because these entries are synthetic anyway and leaving them ungated
  // shows the whole line as available. Chain roots keep
  // the wiki loyalty-level gates as traderRequirements with synthetic ids
  // 'overlay.<placeholder id>.<traderId>.level.>=.N'. Replace both with
  // upstream data when the real IDs land; the issue lists each gate.

